A stray :ENDIF inside a procedure with no block open inside it. The
procedure is a frame, not a block the :ENDIF could be crossing, so this is
unmatched_block_end, not mismatched_block_end, and the :ENDPROC still
closes the procedure cleanly (diag.unmatched_block_end).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE ResetCounter;
	:DECLARE nCount;
	nCount := 0;
	:ENDIF;
	:RETURN nCount;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE ResetCounter;
	:DECLARE nCount;

	nCount := 0;
:ENDIF;

:RETURN nCount;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
4:2-4:8 error unmatched_block_end: Unexpected ':ENDIF' without matching block start
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
4:2-4:8 error unmatched_block_end: Unexpected ':ENDIF' without matching block start
